{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":282310,\"title\":\"Feu\",\"tagline\":\"\",\"overview\":\"In 1979, Sunil Sarkar photographs the Dumurjhaphi massacre. Nearly two decades later, Daniel ventures into the forests of Bhatti (wetlands) in search of those photographs. Godfathers, honey collectors (mouyals), foreign agents, and Bonbibi — a thousand years of stories lie waiting there. Unwittingly, young Daniel finds himself at the very heart of power. The rules of the jungle whisper in his ear — \\\"Reveal your identity! Are you a youth of Delta ?\\\"\",\"posterPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/xIEoQcBq7dTkGOGlCvy7yvHVzLC.jpg\",\"backdropPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/3B5tWfZiWWtLOgh7w18IqIUC9Gy.jpg\",\"youtubeBackdrop\":null,\"anilistBanner\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"year\":2025,\"genres\":[\"Crime\"],\"status\":\"Returning Series\",\"type\":\"tv\",\"totalSeasons\":2,\"totalEpisodes\":16,\"createdBy\":[\"Sukorno Shahed Dhiman\"],\"networks\":[\"Chorki\"],\"countries\":[{\"code\":\"BD\",\"name\":\"Bangladesh\"}],\"lastAirDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"cast\":[{\"id\":3340264,\"name\":\"Sukorno Shahed Dhiman\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":150410,\"name\":\"Chanchal Chowdhury\",\"character\":\"Sunil\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/46ebiphxjeUP4T1JCGp6G4DAyQL.jpg\"}],\"trailers\":[{\"key\":\"bgpDgJkQka0\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"uouCo9PqxVo\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"MW6FXr5I8V4\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"similar\":[],\"seasonNumber\":2,\"seasonName\":\"Complete Saga\",\"seasonOverview\":\"In 1979, Sunil Sarkar photographs the Dumurjhaphi massacre. Nearly two decades later, Daniel ventures into the forests of Bhatti (wetlands) in search of those photographs. Godfathers, honey collectors (mouyals), foreign agents, and Bonbibi — a thousand years of stories lie waiting there. Unwittingly, young Daniel finds himself at the very heart of power. The rules of the jungle whisper in his ear — \\\"Reveal your identity! Are you a youth of Delta ?\\\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mpunngAK3mmlh8jrZwzAz5Rxs50.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Delta to Headquarters\",\"overview\":\"Sunil Sarkar's pen-friend Father Francisco arrives at Mongla Church in year 2002 to work on the biography of Sunil. Parallely, Sunil crossed the border in 1978 to set foot on Dumurjhapi to help Bangladeshi refugees.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/rIHLzKewsxLcpQZYYHahVFi2wDo.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":23},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Look at the date\",\"overview\":\"In 1978, the conflict between Marshal and Roisu, the fierce Raite Party leader in the Sundarbans, reaches a boiling point. To teach Marshal a lesson, Roisu raids his house.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/l9ZN0tKPPkzxZUfOIZkEuad7BdK.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":23},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Tell No One\",\"overview\":\"In 1978, Sunil's photographs documenting the plight of the Dumurjhaphi refugees appear in international newspapers. Indian agents Sharma and Kazi arrive at the Mongla Church. With the help of influential local figures, they put pressure on the Mongla Church to keep Sunil away from Dumurjhaphi.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/gbauEkaNmRYHm92pxJanqTGgJWo.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":25},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Is the father alive?\",\"overview\":\"While searching for the photographs of the Dumurjhampi massacre, Daniel becomes confused. If Sunil is dead, then who sent the letter? And if Sunil is still alive, then who is buried at the church? Whose hands are the photographs actually in? Daniel becomes desperate to meet the mysterious man, Marshal.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/duMW1XIVzXsBbDZU5rmRk6xawQ4.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":21},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"A cross-border issue\",\"overview\":\"The time for the final assault on the Bangladeshi refugees approaches. RAW agents Sharma and Kazi begin their secret preparations. Meanwhile, Sunil takes the side of the refugees and positions himself in Dumurjhaphi. In the middle, Marshal remains neutral.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/bqLcIoQlZaD8JzobtNy7GsjjVPV.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":19},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"The man is melting\",\"overview\":\"To seize Char Marshal, kazi joins forces with a Pakistani-American agent. Kazi sends a recon team to Char Marshal, but the team encounters a superhuman force—resembling a dark shadow of a man, yet not quite human!\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9uX9L4ICwU97QBbPzXJ0FM9TvNp.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":24},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"We need a machine, a machine\",\"overview\":\"Anjan informs Daniel that Sunil was last seen with Marshal. If Sunil returned, Marshal was supposed to come back too! Daniel meets with the economist Mofakkhar. Mofakkhar and Marshal are staunch allies!\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qUFMs0l5t4cb8o3KYvFGN2tP67b.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":22},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"There is uranium on Char Marshal\",\"overview\":\"Having lost brothers, friends, relatives, and children, Marshal takes shelter at the edge of the Sundarbans. Thus, Char Marshal comes into being. Over the next 20 years, Marshal’s forces gain control of the gateway to the Bay of Bengal. Daniel goes into hiding. Whispers spread through the city. Feu (jackals/agents) lurk all around!\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/p8A6nFCfD8eMTO0OeP9sgQvON6z.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":21},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"We’ll Put Out the Fire with Petrol\",\"overview\":\"Over the question of who will hold control of Char Marshal, the men of the Bhatti (wetlands) split apart. As Kazi and Marshal clash, a thousand-year-old question resurfaces: Who does Bhatti belong to? The original inhabitants, their native masters (the Babus), or the foreign sahibs? Who does this land of Bhatti belong to?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/bHXqMSaq4LcKFhnDWgKaGQ6yOeT.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2026-11-11\",\"runtime\":23}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2025-01-30\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}